============================================================
PATCH 13: grid_label_system.py - Nearest Boundary Selection
============================================================
Issue: At corners where BL polygons overlap, insideness
       (both raw and normalized) picks the wrong block.

Fix: Use NEAREST BOUNDARY — among all polygons containing the
     click, pick the one whose edge is CLOSEST to the click.

Why this works:
  At a corner where block A overlaps block B:
  - Click is at B's corner, near B's edge (e.g., 6m from B's edge)
  - A's polygon extends into B's area, so click is far from A's edge (e.g., 37m)
  - Picking the polygon with SMALLEST edge distance → B wins ✓

